  "notes": "Annulus loft along a 7-point polyline: straight body x -60..10 mm, three folds (r 3.0 / 2.0 mm) at 13.5 / 20.5 / 27.5 mm, then a 12 deg kink from x = 27.5 to 60 mm so the head lifts like a bent flex straw.  Inner wall r 1.6 mm (1.4 mm wall, 0.4 mm at the folds) plus a 6-quad ring at each opening, 6 segments, 120 triangles (budget ceiling), one closed genus-1 shell, no boolean.  Body axis at z = 0.0026 m (one apothem) so the flat underside rests on z = 0.  AABB 0.120 x 0.006 x ~0.012 m: the bend is what pushes Z past the row 0.006, and BEND_DEG = 0 restores the straight 6 mm version.  Materials (2026-11-15 upgrade): the barrel is plastic_red, the three accordion folds (x 0.010-0.0275 m) are the white ceramic slot, and the two mouth annuli are the dark ink slot, so the old near-white pair now reads as a red/white striped straw with shadowed openings.",
